                <pb facs="0820" n="688" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg688"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/253: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-01-15T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 15,
                                1927—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>12. Your telegram number 28, sent January 14, 10 a.m. Your position as presented
                    in third paragraph is approved.</p>
                <p>In view of the developments taking place in the Chinese situation and the
                    opposition that is very evident and widespread against the factions now in
                    control at Peking, the opinion of the Department is that the direction of events
                    should be awaited before considering the granting of recognition to any group or
                    faction making a claim that it acts with authority for the whole Chinese
                    people.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
